# Catalog of Comets for Celestia
# Version 1.7.0
#
# All EllipticalOrbit data for comets below were retrieved from
# NASA/JPL's Small Body Database System (SBDB) unless noted
# otherwise:
#
# https://ssd/jpl.nasa.gov/tools/sbdb_lookup.html#/
#
# The lists were divided into three groups, the Periodic Comets
# (<200 years), Long-Period Comets (200-1000 years) and
# Non-Periodic Comets (>1,000 years). Their geometric albedos
# were assumed to be 0.04 unless noted otherwise
#
# Due to the established system of naming comets after their
# discoverers, a large number of these objects are namesakes of
# one another (e.g. ATLAS, Lovejoy, McNaught, NEOWISE etc.) For 
# this SSC file, we only select the most significant comets that
# share the same formal name.
#
# 
# Density estimates for 1P, 17P, 19P, 21P, 29P, C/1983 H1, C/1995 O1, C/1996 B2
# and C/2013 A1 are from Paradowski (2022), Acta Astronomica 72, 141-159
#  "A New Indirect Method of Determining Density of Cometary Nuclei"
#   https://doi.org/10.32023/0001-5237/72.2.4
# 
# Mass and density estimates for 2P, 19P, and 46P are from Sosa, et al. (2009)
#  "Cometary masses derived from non-gravitational forces", MNRAS 393, 192-214
#   https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2966.2008.14183.x
#
# Radius for C/1956 R1 and C/2006 P1 are derived from Equation 1 of
# Fernandez, et al. (2012), MNRAS 423, 1674-1690
#  "Magnitude and size distribution of long-period comets in Earth-crossing or approaching orbits"
#   https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2966.2012.20989.x
#
# Bond and Geometric Albedos for 2P, 19P, 21P, 46P, 55P, 96P, and 153P
# are from Rondon (2025), MNRAS 538, 2869-2904
#  "Secular light curves of periodic comets observed by SWAN/SOHO"
#   https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/staf454
#
#
# Last update: 9 July 2026


"46P Wirtanen:Wirtanen:P 1948 A1:P 1954 R2" "Sol" 
{
	Class	"comet"
	Mesh	"asteroid.cms"
	Texture	"asteroid.jpg"
	Radius	 0.6					# D = 1.2 km
	TailColor	[ 0.30 1.0 0.65 ]
	Mass<kg>	3.3e11
	Density	 400

	EllipticalOrbit
	{
		Epoch        	2458465.500000	# 2018-Dec-13, 00:00
		Period                5.438847265757708
		SemiMajorAxis	      3.092661874753647
		Eccentricity	      0.6587550054889648
		Inclination	         11.7475487582537
		AscendingNode	     82.15763392494087
		ArgOfPericenter	    356.341071857073
		MeanAnomaly	          0.01247351001231614
	}

	# Rotation period from Meech (1997)
	# https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1997A&A...326.1268M

	RotationPeriod	 7.60
	GeomAlbedo		 0.44
	BondAlbedo		 0.4
	InfoURL	"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/46P/Wirtanen"
}
